    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Assaly Cottage is a beautiful country style traditional Irish cottage, with a distinctive part-thatched roof, set on the edge Killinick village, approximately 8km from Wexford Town. The property combines traditional character with spacious and practical living accommodation, making it an attractive home in a well-connected coastal location. Inside, the entrance hall leads directly into an impressive dining room with a double-height vaulted ceiling and mezzanine overlooking, creating a bright and open focal point within the home. To the rear of the property is a spacious open-plan kitchen and dining area with adjoining sitting room, along with a separate utility room. The ground floor also includes an additional sitting room, the primary bedroom, and the main bathroom. Upstairs, there are three further bedrooms together with a large shower room, providing ample space for family living or guest accommodation. Assaly Cottage sits on c. 0.49 acres with ample parking space and a low maintenance rear garden. The property is ideally positioned adjacent to Killinick village and within a short drive of a number of renowned beaches including Rosslare Strand, St. Helens, Carne & Kilmore Quay, only 15km away. Rosslare Europort is approximately five minutes away, while Wexford Town is within easy reach at approximately 8km. The N11/N25 road network is also easily accessible, making commuting and travel convenient. Assaly Cottage off\u001ders excellent opportunity to acquire a character-filled home in a highly sought-after location. Enjoying the benefits of country living while remaining close to all essential amenities and transport links, the property will appeal to a broad range of buyers seeking a permanent residence, holiday home, or investment opportunity.\r\n\r\nVIEWING HIGHLY RECOMMENDED"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall – (1.9m × 1.7m), With a tiled floor\r\nDining room – (6.5m × 3.9m), Tiled floor, vaulted double height ceiling, stove with tiled surround, exposed beam\r\nMezzanine – (3.7m × 6.5m), Overlooking dining room\r\nBedroom 2 – (4.0m × 3.8m), With a vaulted ceiling\r\nInner Hallway – (2.3m × 1m), Tiled floor and fuse box\r\nBedroom 1 (3.4m × 3.2m), With a carpet floor and storage closet\r\nMain Bathroom – (2.1m × 3.3m), Part tiled walls, tiled floor, bath, W/C, WHB, frosted window, step in shower\r\nSitting Room – (3.6m × 3.8m), With a tiled floor & stairs to bedroom 3\r\nKitchen/ Dining room – (4.4m × 5.7m), Tiled floor, exposed beam, waist & eye level cabinets,\r\nSitting Room 2 – (5.8m × 4.8m), With a tiled floor, exposed beams, stove with a feature surround, stairs to bedroom 4 & door to rear patio\r\nUtility Room – (3.6m × 2.1m), Tiled floor, access to rear garden and sitting room 2, plumbed for a washer & dryer\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nBedroom 3 – (3.7m × 3.2m), Vaulted ceiling and carpet floor\r\nBedroom 4 – (5.4m × 4.1m), Carpet floor, vaulted ceiling & eves storage\r\nEn-suite – (2.2m × 2.5m), Lino flooring, frosted window W/C, WHB & step in fully tiled shower\r\nShed – (5m × 7m), With a concrete floor and rolling door\r\n\r\nOutside: Enclosed yard, lawn, concrete patio, shed, ample parking\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating\r\nBER: F Ber No: 119359115 Performance indicator: 423.1 kWh/m2/yr"
      },
